evenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares are roughly flat over the past year excluding the latest month.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 17% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 39% and a beta of 0.99, it moves roughly with the market.","About $35.8M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 52% in the 2020 crash, 31% in the 2022 bear market and 78% in 2008."],"val":["The stock trades only 1% below its DCF fair value of $295, a thin margin of safety.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 45%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $220 to $401 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Industrials peers: P/E 29.5 vs 23.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 20% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 4.5% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 4.1% (vs the 8% bar).","The 2 covering analysts target $358 on average, 22% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 14% earns above the cost of capital of 9.1%, but the 5pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have been steady (CV 0.23).","It converts 15% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.68x.","ROE of 10% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.7x equity multiplier).","It spends 1.5% of revenue on R&D and 1.1% on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 1.2x net debt to EBITDA ($119.6M of cash against $374.5M of debt), with interest covered 10.1x.","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.38).","Working capital ties up about 152 days of sales, a drag on cash generation."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 5.2% over 3 years, 10.6% over 5 years and 10.4% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating.","At current returns, reinvesting 25% of profits supports about 3.5% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 12.6% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 0.99, a backlog worth 3% of annual revenue and deferred revenue up 12%.","Capex runs only 0.3x depreciation (1.6% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 24, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.7%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Shareholder yield is a modest 0.3% (0.5% in dividends, less 0.1% of net share issuance).","It has paid a dividend for 12 consecutive years, raising it 7.7% a year over the last five.","Short interest is elevated at 11.9% of the float, 5.9 days to cover."],"people":["With about 4,000 employees, each generates about $263K of revenue, 0.7x the Industrials median, and productivity has risen 8.5% a year.","That works out to $39K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.5M (9x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (3/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $3K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":73,"head":"Watch: LEAN BUY-rated, but only 1% below fair value; it becomes a buy below $251.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 48, gates 13/25)","FCF margin 14.7%","Revenue grew 10.6%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA 1.2x","Altman Z in the safe zone"],"cons":["P/E 29.5x vs sector 23.3x"],"flags":[],"need":["only 1% below fair value"],"buy_below":250.53,"vc":{"base":294.74,"base_src":"dcf","bear":220.37,"bull":401.38,"alt_median":98.84,"n_alt":3,"gap":1.9821,"dispersion":0.4491,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (45% dispersion)","DCF is 198% above the other models' median ($98.84)"]},"med":{"pe":23.2692,"ev_ebitda":13.319,"pfcf":22.2778,"pb":3.0551,"roic":0.1001,"gross_margin":0.2851,"fcf_margin":0.068,"div_yield":0.0147}},"ticker":"KAI","date":"2026-11-06"}